<title>FINLAND: Silja says passengers up 6 pct in '96.</title>
<headline>Silja says passengers up 6 pct in '96.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish passenger ferry operator Silja Line, part of Silja Oy Ab, said on Tuesday its passenger volume rose about six percent year-on-year in 1996 to 5.9 million passengers.</p>
<p>&quot;In 1996, Silja Line carried a record number of passengers, 5.9 million or about six percent more than in 1995,&quot; Silja Line said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The number of private cars carried rose more than ten percent year-on-year to about 385,000 cars, and the number of cargo units rose almost 17 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Silja gave the following figures:</p>
<p> Passengers			     1996	    1995   Change pct</p>
<p> Helsinki-Stockholm		1,331,781     1,357,543    -1.9</p>
<p> Turku-Stockholm		   2,050,223     2,070,616    -0.9</p>
<p>Maarianhamina- Stockholm/Turku    99,267	  83,666   +18.6</p>
<p>Vaasa-Uumaja			   736,908	 599,734   +22.9</p>
<p>Vaasa-Sundsvall			    598	 278,968   -99.8</p>
<p>Pietarsaari-Skelleftea	     127,698	  89,334   +42.9</p>
<p>Helsinki-Tallinn		   1,337,572	 885,624   +52.8</p>
<p>Helsinki-Travemunde		  220,815	 208,005    +6.2</p>
<p>Total				  5,904,862     5,573,490    +5.9</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
</text>
